      "text": "We drop our MIPS target because it no longer works.[1] We were previously using it as a means of testing ripgrep in a big endian environment.",
      "files": [
        "tests/feature.rs",
        "tests/misc.rs",
        "tests/util.rs"
      ],
      "commit": "3bfa125b2ea8175947360322f1429a0205be6c76",
      "split": "holdout",
      "state": "live",
      "survival": 0.97
    },
    {
      "id": "f3bfa125b-1",
      "kind": "decision",
      "text": "ci: replace mips with powerpc64, aarch64 and s390x",
      "files": [
        "tests/feature.rs",
        "tests/misc.rs",
        "tests/util.rs"
      ],
      "commit": "3bfa125b2ea8175947360322f1429a0205be6c76",
      "split": "holdout",
      "state": "live",
      "survival": 0.97
    },
    {
      "id": "f6cdb99ea-0",
      "kind": "gotcha",
      "text": "I did this because the marginal cost of adding the Iterator::count() specialization to memchr was extremely small.",
      "files": [
        "crates/searcher/src/lines.rs"
      ],
      "commit": "6cdb99ea61d585cc32716d181517d71b4df769b5",
      "split": "tune",
      "state": "unknown",
      "survival": 1.0
    },
    {
      "id": "f6cdb99ea-1",
      "kind": "decision",
      "text": "As of the memchr 2.6 release, its Iterator::count method is specialized to only count the number of occurrences instead of finding the offset of each occurrence.",
      "files": [
        "crates/searcher/src/lines.rs"
      ],
      "commit": "6cdb99ea61d585cc32716d181517d71b4df769b5",
      "split": "tune",
      "state": "unknown",
      "survival": 1.0
    },
    {
      "id": "fd938e955-0",
      "kind": "gotcha",
      "text": "But it turns out that a naive stack-behind-a-mutex can be quite a bit slower than something that's a little smarter, such as a work-stealing stack used in this commit.",
      "files": [
        "crates/ignore/src/walk.rs"
      ],
      "commit": "d938e955af7a39ac0245b1ce84924f7f4a2141ac",
      "split": "holdout",
      "state": "live",
      "survival": 0.86
    },
    {
      "id": "f23e21133-0",
      "kind": "gotcha",
      "text": "I originally did not put PathPrinter into grep-printer because I considered it somewhat extraneous to what a \"grep\" program does, and also that its implementation was rather simple.",
      "files": [
        "crates/core/args.rs",
        "crates/core/main.rs",
        "crates/core/path_printer.rs",
        "crates/printer/src/hyperlink.rs",
        "crates/printer/src/lib.rs",
        "crates/printer/src/path.rs",
        "crates/printer/src/standard.rs",
        "crates/printer/src/summary.rs",
        "crates/printer/src/util.rs"
      ],
      "commit": "23e21133ba6a8ca2c4d040092ad1bc22f14e8861",
      "split": "holdout",
      "state": "unknown",
      "survival": 0.76
    },
    {
      "id": "ff608d4d9-0",
      "kind": "gotcha",
      "text": "I want this because I know at least for my own use cases, I sometimes log into systems using an SSH hostname that is distinct from the system's actual hostname (usually because the system is shared in some way or changing its hostname is not allowed/practical).",
      "files": [
        "crates/core/app.rs",
        "crates/core/args.rs",
        "crates/printer/src/hyperlink.rs",
        "crates/printer/src/hyperlink_aliases.rs",
        "crates/printer/src/lib.rs",
        "crates/printer/src/path.rs",
        "crates/printer/src/standard.rs",
        "crates/printer/src/summary.rs",
        "crates/printer/src/util.rs"
      ],
      "commit": "f608d4d9b3ab210b7e6964ca7d1d7dc9c077329e",
      "split": "holdout",
      "state": "live",
      "survival": 0.83
    },
    {
      "id": "ff608d4d9-1",
      "kind": "decision",
      "text": "The biggest change is probably requiring the caller to pass in things like a hostname instead of having the crate do it.",
      "files": [
        "crates/core/app.rs",
        "crates/core/args.rs",
        "crates/printer/src/hyperlink.rs",
        "crates/printer/src/hyperlink_aliases.rs",
        "crates/printer/src/lib.rs",
        "crates/printer/src/path.rs",
        "crates/printer/src/standard.rs",
        "crates/printer/src/summary.rs",
        "crates/printer/src/util.rs"
      ],
      "commit": "f608d4d9b3ab210b7e6964ca7d1d7dc9c077329e",
      "split": "holdout",
      "state": "live",
      "survival": 0.83
    },
    {
      "id": "f7f456404-0",
      "kind": "decision",
      "text": "It also inlines the dozen or so lines of code for FNV hashing instead of bringing in a micro-crate for it.",
      "files": [
        "crates/globset/src/fnv.rs",
        "crates/globset/src/glob.rs",
        "crates/globset/src/lib.rs",
        "crates/globset/src/pathutil.rs"
      ],
      "commit": "7f456404010005142a6493fb48bd9fd06aca2731",
      "split": "tune",
      "state": "live",
      "survival": 0.96
    },
    {
      "id": "f88524a2b-0",
      "kind": "gotcha",
      "text": "Because of that, we can dedup the patterns via just their concrete syntax without any fuss.",
      "files": [
        "crates/core/args.rs"
      ],
      "commit": "88524a2b5232c951f9d4c0a169a046a7354251bd",
      "split": "holdout",
      "state": "stale",
      "survival": 0.0
    },
    {
      "id": "fc21302b4-0",
      "kind": "gotcha",
      "text": "It turns out that the presence of a Unicode word boundary can defeat acceleration to a point.",
      "files": [
        "crates/regex/src/literal.rs"
      ],
      "commit": "c21302b4096f9ce1af095fbe8b14828a90ecfecb",
      "split": "tune",
      "state": "live",
      "survival": 1.0
    },
    {
      "id": "febb986e7-0",
      "kind": "gotcha",
      "text": "The failure mode here is still pretty bad because you need to know to reach for the `--debug` flag in the first place.",
      "files": [
        "crates/core/flags/hiargs.rs"
      ],
      "commit": "ebb986e767655f8c9c05a7a7e99b09236a6e8be5",
      "split": "holdout",
      "state": "live",
      "survival": 1.0
    },
    {
      "id": "f286de956-0",
      "kind": "gotcha",
      "text": "Essentially, --version now subsumes --pcre2-version, although we do retain the former because it (usefully) emits an exit code based on whether PCRE2 is available or not.",
      "files": [
        "crates/core/flags/doc/version.rs",
        "crates/core/flags/mod.rs",
        "crates/core/main.rs"
      ],
      "commit": "286de9564e511f01f13756c207e9b26ec781591d",
      "split": "tune",
      "state": "live",
      "survival": 1.0
    },
    {
      "id": "f9ed7565f-0",
      "kind": "gotcha",
      "text": "Basically, unless the -a/--text flag is given, it is generally always an error to search for an explicit NUL byte because the binary detection will prevent it from matching.",
      "files": [
        "crates/core/flags/hiargs.rs",
        "crates/regex/src/ban.rs",
        "crates/regex/src/config.rs",
        "crates/regex/src/error.rs",
        "crates/regex/src/lib.rs",
        "crates/regex/src/matcher.rs",
        "crates/searcher/src/line_buffer.rs",
        "crates/searcher/src/searcher/mod.rs",
        "tests/regression.rs"
      ],
      "commit": "9ed7565fcb47d02e76398d41f24ba0817f6b9c2f",
      "split": "holdout",
      "state": "live",
      "survival": 1.0
    }
